# Archived snapshot: `historical/previous_implementations/PaperFormalization.lean`

The original text of this file is preserved verbatim in the git history:

    git show b4001a7:historical/previous_implementations/PaperFormalization.lean

(sha256 `7254a715c77596d4ebda37dd3443b03814351661ddecb38a0969844b01c74649`, listed in `historical/ARCHIVED_LEAN_SNAPSHOTS.md`).

That text was never compiled by the kernel-certificate build: it was outside the lake
libraries, and it contained 3 uses of `sorry`/`axiom` outside comments. It proves nothing and is not part of any claim.

This file now contains only this note, so that every tracked `.lean` file is compiled with
no `sorry` and no custom axiom. The kernel-checked development is the `NS_Millennium_Proof`
library; see `README.md`.
